{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"xpath\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"count\" expr=\"0\"/>\n    <data id=\"done\" expr=\"false()\"/>\n    <data id=\"user\"><name xmlns=\"\">bob</name></data>\n  </datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"inc\"><assign location=\"3\" expr=\"1\"/></transition>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-location-not-a-path.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml039-xpath-location-not-a-path.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":48,"endLine":8,"startColumn":47,"startLine":8}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`location` is not an assignable xpath location: `3` selects no node, so nothing can be assigned to it\n\n**Note:** an XPath location must select existing nodes: a declared variable `$name` or a path below it such as `$name/child` or `$name/@attribute`; `a.b` is one variable name that contains a dot, and `a[0]` is a predicate, not an index\n\n**Help:** write a `$`-rooted path to a declared `<data>` variable, such as `$count` or `$order/item/@qty`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML CR 2014 §C.3 The XPath Data Model","text":"`location` is not an assignable xpath location: `3` selects no node, so nothing can be assigned to it"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":307,"start":306},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML039"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`location`, `idlocation`, `namelist` items, and `<foreach item/index>` must name an assignable place; SCXML 1.0 defines the run-time outcome of one that does not, so the document compiles: §5.9.2 \"If a location expression cannot be evaluated to yield a valid location, the SCXML processor MUST place the error 'error.execution' in the internal event queue\", and §4.6 \"if 'item' does not specify a legal variable name, the SCXML processor MUST terminate execution of the <foreach> element and the block that contains it, and place the error error.execution on the internal event queue\". In ECMAScript an assignable place is a variable or a property access such as `data.field` or `data[0]`; in XPath it is an expression that selects existing nodes, such as `$data` or `$data/field` (`a.b` is one variable name containing a dot, and `a[0]` is a predicate)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: ECMAScript: use a variable name or a member expression such as `data.field`; XPath: use a `$`-rooted path to a declared variable such as `$data/field`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML039` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LocationExpressions","id":"SCXML039","name":"SCXML039","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a location is not assignable in the selected data model"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}